      "dom_id": "question-54386",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ radians to an equivalent measure in degrees. This gives\n\n$$\n(\\frac{\\pi }{6})(\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi })=\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{6}={30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since we know that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$",
